{
  "version": "1.1",
  "description": "STING LOD verification matrix. Corporate baseline; merged by id over a project overlay at <project>/_BIM_COORD/lod_matrix.json (project milestones/categoryRules win by id/category). Checks are a PARAMETER + NAMING + GEOMETRY-PRESENCE maturity proxy, NOT a geometric survey — STING cannot verify that geometry is dimensionally correct, only that it exists, is not a placeholder family, and carries the parameters expected at that LOD. Per-LOD check fields: requireGeometry (non-degenerate bbox), forbidPlaceholderFamilies (family/type name must not match placeholderFamilyPatterns), requiredParams (shared param present + non-empty; '+name' adds to the inherited list, a plain name replaces it), requiredDims (numeric shared param resolves > 0), requireTypeNotGeneric (type/family name must not contain 'generic'), requireManufacturerType (type+family name must not match a placeholder pattern — manufacturer-specified proxy), requireNoUnresolvedClash (NOT API-verifiable — reported as an INFO limitation, never a hard fail), inherit (LOD key to inherit checks from). LADDER: the full standard 100/200/300/350/400/500 ladder is defined for every category. LOD 100 is the conceptual rung — the element is modelled and categorised, nothing more — so its check block is deliberately empty and every in-scope element passes it; it exists so the ladder is complete and a project overlay can bind a milestone to it.  Every parameter named below exists in MR_PARAMETERS.txt with a GUID and is bound <ALL> in RESOLVED_BINDINGS.csv — a required param that is not in the shared-parameter file would make the check permanently unsatisfiable. NOTE: ASS_INSTALLATION_DATE_TXT is the canonical install-date parameter; ASS_INSTALL_DATE_TXT is marked DEPRECATED in MR_PARAMETERS.txt and must not be used here. No milestone is bound to LOD 100 because no contract deliverable sits there; add one in a project overlay if a project needs it. RUNG 500 DIFFERS BY CATEGORY, DELIBERATELY. LOD 500 is field-verified as-built. On SERIALISED, SERVICEABLE PLANT — Mechanical Equipment, Electrical Equipment, Plumbing Fixtures, Lighting Fixtures, Air Terminals, Sprinklers, Fire Alarm Devices, Specialty Equipment — it inherits 400 and adds +ASS_SERIAL_NR_TXT and +ASS_INSTALLATION_DATE_TXT, because that is the O&M/commissioning record the Owner actually receives and what Fohlio publishes. On BUILDING FABRIC AND DISTRIBUTION — Walls, Floors, Doors, Windows, Roofs, Ceilings, Stairs, Railings, Ramps, Curtain Panels, Curtain Wall Mullions, Ducts, Pipes, Duct/Pipe Fittings, Conduits, Cable Trays, Structural Framing/Columns/Foundations, Casework, Electrical Fixtures, Rooms, and the \"*\" fallback — rung 500 is a bare inherit of 400 and adds NO required parameters. An installation date on every wall, duct run and pipe segment is not something a general contractor's as-built delivers; demanding it would make the first deliverable-d run report near-total failure on fabric and train the team to ignore the report. The rung still means something on fabric — it carries 400's manufacturer/model requirements — it just stops demanding data nobody produces. On FF&E — Furniture and Furniture Systems — rung 500 sits between the two: it inherits 400 and adds +ASS_INSTALLATION_DATE_TXT and +FOHLIO_REF_TXT, but NOT a serial number. Fohlio is the Owner's FF&E single source of truth and publishes the end-of-project O&M manuals, so a dated install and a live Fohlio link are exactly what handover carries for a furniture item; a per-item serial number is not. This is also what makes the LOD gate and Fohlio_Audit agree at Deliverable D instead of reporting different answers about the same register. Doors and Windows are deliberately in the FABRIC group: they carry manufacturer and model at 400 and are schedule-tracked, but they are not serialised plant. SCOPE: project-wide LOD_Verify collects every taggable model category (LodScope.Collect), so the \"*\" rule is genuinely reachable, and the run DISCLOSES the categories it did not scan in the TaskDialog, the CSV header and the JSON gate report.",
  "milestones": [
    { "id": "deliverable-a", "name": "Deliverable A (Basis of Design)", "lod": 200 },
    { "id": "deliverable-b", "name": "Deliverable B (50% documentation)", "lod": 300 },
    { "id": "deliverable-c", "name": "Deliverable C (100% documentation)", "lod": 350 },
    { "id": "conformed-set", "name": "Conformed set", "lod": 350 },
    { "id": "construction", "name": "Construction stage (fabrication/installation)", "lod": 400 },
    { "id": "deliverable-d", "name": "Deliverable D (record / as-built model)", "lod": 500 }
  ],
  "placeholderFamilyPatterns": [
    "(?i)placeholder",
    "(?i)^STING_SEED_",
    "(?i)\\bTBD\\b",
    "(?i)\\bdummy\\b",
    "<[^>]*>"
  ],
